    "result_text": "I implemented `build_client` in `app/llm_client.py`, and all four ops requirements work. The test suite passes (1 test), and I also checked the behaviour with a stub transport that always returns HTTP 500.\n\n**Installed versions differ from what you might expect.** The pinned `openai==3.19.2` uses `httpx2` instead of `httpx`. I checked the Context7 docs and the installed source to confirm it, so the code uses `httpx2` and the SDK's `DefaultHttpx2Client`. No dependencies were added.\n\n**What `build_client` does:**\n1. **Timeouts:** sets `httpx2.Timeout(30.0, connect=5.0)`, which gives connect 5s and read/write/pool 30s. I set it on both the HTTP client and `OpenAI(timeout=...)`. The SDK sends its own timeout with every request, so setting it only on the HTTP client isn't reliable.\n2. **Retries:** `max_retries=2`.\n3. **Logging:** a `request` event hook logs `\"<METHOD> <URL>\"` at INFO on the `app.http` logger. The SDK sends each retry through the HTTP client again, so every attempt gets logged.\n4. **Transport:** when `transport` is given, it is passed to the HTTP client; otherwise the default is used.\n\n**Stub-transport check:** one `models.list()` call made 3 attempts (the first plus 2 retries). Each attempt logged `GET https://api.openai.com/v1/models` on `app.http`. Each request carried the timeout `{'connect': 5.0, 'read': 30.0, 'write': 30.0, 'pool': 30.0}`, and the call ended with `InternalServerError`.\n\n**Cleanup needed:** I couldn't delete my scratch script `_check_client.py` from the project root because deleting it needed approval. Please remove it, or let me know and I'll do it."
